  "transport": [
    {"t": "From the airport", "d": "Disney's free Magical Express ended in January 2022. Mears Connect, which absorbed The Sunshine Flyer in 2023, is the shared bus: about $17 to $21 an adult and $14 a child each way in 2025, so roughly $250 each way for our crew. Its Express service was $250 round trip for 4 plus $55 per extra rider. A rideshare is about $40 a car, a taxi $60 to $80, and a private car $75 to $150 each way. Minnie Vans cost $199 each way plus tax, seat 6 and serve Deluxe resort guests."},
    {"t": "Car seats", "d": "Mears buses do not need car seats, but its vans do not supply them. Uber's car-seat option has one seat, for children over 2. Minnie Vans carry two seats, and airport Minnie Vans up to three. Quicksilver private cars include car seats and boosters at about $120 each way in 2025. For August, we bring his own seat."},
    {"t": "Disney's free transport", "d": "Buses run from every Disney hotel to all four parks, from 45 minutes before opening until an hour after closing. The Skyliner links Art of Animation, Pop Century, Caribbean Beach and Riviera with EPCOT and Hollywood Studios. The monorail links the Contemporary, Polynesian and Grand Floridian with Magic Kingdom and EPCOT. Boats serve Magic Kingdom, EPCOT, Hollywood Studios and Disney Springs from certain hotels. On boats, strollers must be folded."},
    {"t": "Parking", "d": "Overnight self-parking is free at Disney's own hotels, and their guests park free at the parks. Everyone else pays $35 a car per day at the theme parks, or $50 to $60 for closer spots. Valet at Disney hotels is $42 a night. The Swan and Dolphin charge $40 a day to self-park. Parking at the water parks and Disney Springs is free."},
    {"t": "Flying with August", "d": "Check the airline's lap infant rules; we have not confirmed them. Disney's advice is to gate-check strollers and car seats so they are waiting when we land. Disney's Airport Luggage Transfer sends checked bags from Orlando International to value and moderate resorts for American, JetBlue, Southwest and United flights. Allow up to 4 hours for bags to arrive."},
    {"t": "Groceries", "d": "Villas and cabins have full kitchens, and family suites have a kitchenette with a fridge and microwave. Quicksilver includes a free 30-minute grocery stop on the way from the airport if we ask ahead. WDW Prep School suggests placing a delivery order the day before we leave. We have not compared delivery services yet."}
  ],
  "parksLede": "Four theme parks, each a full day or more. Magic Kingdom is the one for little kids, with the most rides that have no height rule.",
  "littleLede": "Disney World is big and hot, so the plan for August is short park mornings, a real nap, and a pool.",
  "diningLede": "Dining reservations open 60 days ahead at 6 a.m. Eastern, and character meals go first.",
